course: dictionary
lesson: 3313
title: Words that tell you where
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and those parts give clues. Eurasian comes from Europe and Asia joined together, so Eurasian means about both of those places at once.
explain: «The Eurasian lynx lives in the Carpathians and Polissia, is rare and protected.» Eurasian is part of the animal's name, so it tells you where the lynx belongs. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this name? A place that covers Europe and Asia together.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The Eurasian eagle owl is one of the biggest owls.» Does it still make sense to say it is an owl from Europe and Asia? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: Eurasian means about Eurasia, the land of Europe and Asia together.
fact: Eurasia is one of the biggest pieces of land on Earth.
fact: Many animal names use Eurasian to show where they live, like the Eurasian otter and the Eurasian jay.
fact: The Eurasian plate is a huge piece of the Earth's crust under Europe and Asia.
fact: Long ago, a Eurasian was a person with one European parent and one Asian parent; this use is dated and old-fashioned today.
exercise: What does Eurasia mean? | Africa and South America together | The biggest desert on Earth | *Europe and Asia together | A very cold ocean
exercise: «Its tall ear tufts are only feathers, not ears.» What are the owl's ear tufts? | Hard grey claws | *Only feathers, not ears | Its real ears, folded up tight | Two small wings
exercise: Find and copy the word from «The Eurasian lynx lives in the Carpathians and Polissia» that tells you where the lynx lives. | *Eurasian | protected | rare | lynx
test: What does the Eurasian otter tell you? | It is an otter that can fly | *It is an otter that lives across Europe and Asia | It is an otter with very short fur | It is an otter that lives at the South Pole
test: Why do animals like the Eurasian blue tit have Eurasian in their names? | Because they are very fast | Because they were found on a ship | Because they have blue ears | *Because they live across Europe and Asia
exam: «The Eurasian eagle owl, with wings almost two metres across, can catch hares.» What does Eurasian tell you? | The owl is a fish from the Arctic | Eurasian is a kind of tree | *The owl lives across Europe and Asia | The owl's wings are about two centimetres across
